.TH DIFTRAYWM-COMMANDS 7
.SH NAME
commands - selected DiftrayWM Command Bar commands
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
:spawn above|below
Create a terminal cell adjacent to the focused cell.
.TP
:mux split horizontal|vertical
Split the focused multiplexer pane below (horizontal) or beside it (vertical).
Shortcuts are Meta+S and Meta+V.
.TP
:mux focus next|prev|up|down|left|right
Move multiplexer focus. Meta+O cycles forward, Meta+P cycles back, and
Meta+Ctrl with an arrow key moves directionally.
.TP
:mux kill
Remove the focused multiplexer pane. The last pane is kept.
.TP
:mux zoom
Expand the focused pane to a TCursor and back. Shortcut is Meta+Z.
.TP
:mux list
List multiplexer panes with the focused one marked *.
.TP
:keymap show
Print the loaded keymap INI, its profiles, the active profile and every binding.
:keymap reload re-reads the file and keeps the previous keymap on a parse error.
:keymap check <path> validates a candidate file without adopting it.
:keymap profile <name> switches profile; :keymap reset returns to the default.
:keymap chord <spec> validates a chord such as <C-q> and reports its key code.
See :help keymap.
.TP
:cell select|focus|promote|restore
Operate on the selected terminal cell.
.TP
:tab next|prev
Cycle NCursor or GCursor tabs.
.TP
:workspace {1-10}
Switch workspaces.
.TP
:cursor list ids
List live graphical cursor identifiers.
.TP
:help {page}
Open a manual page. `help diftrayctl` documents the diftrayctl utility.
.TP
:plugin load|unload {path}
Load or unload a native plugin shared library. diftrayctl plugin-load.
.TP
:plugin list
List loaded plugins.
.TP
:extension exec {path}
Load and run a Lua extension. diftrayctl extension-exec.
.TP
:extension list
List loaded extensions.
.TP
:script source {path.tsc}
Run a Termscript file and show its output. diftrayctl source-script.
.TP
:terminal script {path.tsc}
Run a Termscript program against the active terminal cell. Load
"diftray.terminal" with G:load, then use screen(), cursor(), size(),
display(text), send(text), and running(). Other Termscript standard library
modules are available. screen() returns the visible Unicode text, cursor()
returns zero-based "row,column", and size() returns "rows,columns".
display(text) renders without sending to the shell; send(text) writes to its
PTY and returns false if the cell has no running PTY.
.TP
:launcher lock|unlock|toggle
Lock the launch bar to the top of the screen, release it, or flip the state.
diftrayctl lock-launchbar, unlock-launchbar, toggle-launchbar.
.TP
:launcher status
Report the launch bar's lock state, anchor, height and visibility.
.TP
:session status
Report session, cell, plugin, extension, config and theme state.
.TP
:session exit
Leave the session and return to the Linux console. diftrayctl exit-session.
.TP
:session restart
Re-execute the compositor in place. diftrayctl restart-session.
.TP
:config path
Print the configuration file in use.
.TP
:config open
Open the configuration file in $EDITOR. diftrayctl config-open.
.TP
:config reload
Re-read the configuration file. Reloads atomically.
.TP
:theme load {file.css}
Apply a CSS theme file. See themes/default.css and themes/light.css.
.TP
:theme show
List the active theme properties.
.TP
:set theme :root { ... }
Apply inline CSS theme properties.

.TP
:output list
List logical monitor geometry and the focused output.
.TP
:output focus {name|next|prev}
Focus a monitor. Meta+[ and Meta+] cycle monitors.
.TP
:output move {name}
Move the active NCursor and its graphical clients to a monitor.
.TP
:ncursor list|new
List NCursor and cell IDs, or create an NCursor on the focused monitor.
.TP
:cell move {cell-id} {ncursor-id}
Move a cell, including Notelet state and owned graphical clients.
.TP
:cursor move {cursor-id} cell|ncursor {destination-id}
Change a graphical cursor's ownership, preserving its docked state.
.TP
:output rotate {name} {0|90|180|270}
Rotate a connected output counter-clockwise. Focus and cells are preserved.
.TP
:output scale {name} {0.5-4}
Set output scale, including fractional values such as 1.25.
.TP
:output position {name} {x} {y}
Set monitor placement in logical desktop coordinates. Negative values are allowed.
.TP
:output position {name} auto
Restore automatic placement. Output overrides last for this compositor session.

.TP
:config vars
List typed configuration variables.
.TP
:config eval {expression}
Evaluate a configuration function, macro, or expression and display its value.
.TP
:config run {expression}
Execute a returned command string or command list in this bar's scope.
For example: config run notebook("scratchpad").
